1|0@AskReddit^1440435079#cue1rg4:EmzieM$:A hurley is [this thing] (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hurley_(stick)) and is used to hit a slíotar (the ball). Hurling the fastest game on land and it basically consists of getting the sliothar into the net (for a goal) or over the bar (for a point) using the hurleys. There's no reason why Setanta was so good at hurling except that he was just really athletically talented. He used the hurley and the slíotar to kill the fearsome guard dog of Cullan and then had to serve the role of guardian until a replacement could be found which is how he become known as Cú Chulainn which means 'Hound of Cullan'. 
1|0@AskReddit^1440431505#cudzhev:mynameisrainer$:I've been exploring the wide world of sports and I think the Hurley you are talking about is actually [Hurling](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8i3-Qk7FNeQ). It seems pretty neat, but I'm still kinda lost on how it really works. As for the 2nd part of your question, I have no clue. 
1|0@AskReddit^1440432198#cudzx59:EnidColeslawSideEye$:Hurley is actually the name of the stick used in hurling: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hurley_(stick) And hurling is rad! It's like a mix between soccer (played on a pitch and you can score by getting the ball in the goal), american football (you can also score by hitting the ball through uprights) and lacrosse (you use the hurley to run with the ball balanced on the end of the stick). This video has clips of the primary rules: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fgEMvRrOCRI
