5|0@AskReddit^1440438243#cue3tl1:EmzieM$:People were very, very angry about airports in the West being used by Americans during the Iraq war and many saw it as bullying by the US *telling* us that they were using our airports/cowardice from our own government for not putting their foot down and standing up for our neutrality. We were supposed to be neutral but we were facilitating the refueling of air crafts that were dropping bombs in Iraq. Imagine if we had let the Iraqis stop in Ireland to refuel before continuing on to bomb the US? (Not that Iraq ever bombed the US) It would never have been allowed so therefore we weren't being properly neutral. As always though, despite the fact that the majority of people didn't want them landing there we had no say over the situation and the US continued to do it and our useless government continued to let them. People saw refusing to serve the soldiers as the only kind of protest they had at their disposal. They were angry at the situation not all Americans or all soldiers so they didn't hate *you*. Also, that old woman spitting on you: every country has a few nuts and zealots unfortunately. Try visiting again - even in the cammies - and no one would mind anymore. Hopefully it would be a better experience! 
