1|0@AskReddit^1440435317#cue1x1a:PrahaPrincess$:We have a lot of laws in place to try cut down on our drinking habits. E.g. you can't buy drink before 10am/12pm or after 10pm in shops, can't serve alcohol in pubs/clubs late unless you have a late licence, even then I think 2.30am is the cut-off. We also can't have ''Happy Hours'' or certain drink specials to curtail binge drinking. It's all a reaction to our drinking issues, but it's not really effective- we just work around them.
3|0@AskReddit^1440434568#cue1fgu:PotatoManPerson$:Yeah, were not *that* bad with drinking haha. Our stereotype isn't that true really
